    {
      "id": "hex",
      "title": "joy of hex",
      "layoutId": "standard",
      "tags": [
        "page"
      ],
      "includes": [
        "common-footer"
      ],
      "zones": {
        "title": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "html": "joy of hex"
          }
        ],
        "main": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "html": "\n        <style>\n            #center {\n                position: absolute;\n                top: 50%;\n                left: 50%;\n                border: solid 1px black;\n                width: 0px;\n                height: 0px;\n            }\n            #hex1 {\n                font-size: 30px;\n                animation: wobble 3s infinite;\n                animation-delay: 200ms;\n            }\n            #hex1, #hex1:before, #hex1:after {\n                background-color: #ccc;\n            }\n            #hex2 {\n                font-size: 20px;\n                animation: wobble 3s infinite;\n                animation-delay: 100ms;\n            }\n            #hex2, #hex2:before, #hex2:after {\n                background-color: #999;\n            }\n            #hex3 {\n                font-size: 10px;\n                animation: wobble 3s infinite;\n                animation-delay: 0ms;\n            }\n            #hex3, #hex3:before, #hex3:after {\n                background-color: #666;\n            }\n            .hex {\n                position: absolute;\n                left: -0.5em;\n                top: -0.87em;\n                border-width: 0.1px;\n                border-width: 0;\n                border-style: solid none;\n                width: 1em;\n                height: 1.74em;\n            }\n            .hex:before {\n                content: \"\";\n                position: absolute;\n                border: inherit;\n                width: 100%;\n                height: 100%;\n                transform: rotate(-60deg);\n            }\n            .hex:after {\n                content: \"\";\n                position: absolute;\n                border: inherit;\n                width: 100%;\n                height: 100%;\n                transform: rotate(60deg);\n            }\n            @keyframes wobble {\n                0% { transform: rotate(-90deg); transition: ease-in-out; }\n                50% { transform: rotate(90deg); transition: ease-in-out; }\n                100% { transform: rotate(-90deg); transition: ease-in-out; }\n            }\n        </style>\n        <div class=\"w3-display-container w3-padding-64\">\n            <div class=\"w3-display-middle\">\n                <div id=\"hex1\" class=\"hex\"></div>\n                <div id=\"hex2\" class=\"hex\"></div>\n                <div id=\"hex3\" class=\"hex\"></div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    "
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "home",
      "title": "ineffable",
      "layoutId": "standard",
      "tags": [
        "page"
      ],
      "includes": [
        "common-footer"
      ],
      "zones": {
        "title": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "html": "ineffable"
          }
        ],
        "main": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "html": "<p class='w3-dark-grey w3-padding-small'>TOP OF PAGE</p><div class=\"w3-row-padding w3-stretch\"><div class=\"w3-twothird \"><h2>Welcome to the first rec-tem website</h2><p>This is also my first responsive website. I was going to be good and build it myself, but W3CSS is so good that it was daft not to make use of it.</p><p>Next is to convert Millers Ark and see if I can make it look attractive.</p></div><div class=\"w3-third w3-padding-16\">\n                <div class=\"w3-display-container w3-container w3-padding-16 w3-card w3-center undefined\">\n                    <img src=\"./img/img1.jpg\" class=\"w3-image\" style=\"width: 100%\">\n                    \n                        <div class=\"w3-display-middle w3-container w3-padding-16 w3-display-hover w3-normal w3-round-large w3-opacity-min w3-white w3-text-white\">This is not my picture.</div>\n                        <div class=\"w3-display-middle w3-container w3-padding-16 w3-display-hover w3-normal w3-animate-opacity w3-text-black\">This is not my picture.</div>\n                        \n                </div>\n            </div></div>\n                <div class=\"w3-content w3-padding-16\" style=\"max-width: 70%\">\n                    <div class=\"w3-panel w3-card-4 w3-round-large w3-sand\">\n                        <p class=\"w3-left-align\"><i class=\"fa fa-quote-left w3-xlarge w3-text-black w3-opacity-max\"></i></p>\n                        <p class=\" w3-xlarge w3-serif w3-center\">good things come to those who code</p>\n                        <p class=\"w3-right-align\"><i class=\"fa fa-quote-right w3-xlarge w3-text-black w3-opacity-max\"></i></p>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            \n                <div class=\"w3-section w3-cell-row\">\n                    <div class=\"w3-cell w3-container w3-mobile w3-teal\"><h3>OMG</h3><p>This is shaping up extremely well.</p><p>This might actually be a viable solution for a statically edited, dynamically rendered site.</p></div><div class=\"w3-cell w3-container w3-mobile w3-orange\"><h3>TO DO</h3><a href='#rectem'>see rec-tem page</a></div><div class=\"w3-cell w3-container w3-mobile w3-light-blue\"><h3>EDITOR</h3><p>This is a departure from the PurplceCms edit-in-place approach, so it will need a new editor.</p><p>I am thinking of a single AWS-hosted editor for all sites, with the data crunched down to static files.</p></div>\n                </div>\n            <p class='w3-dark-grey w3-padding-small'>BOTTOM OF PAGE</p>"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "musings",
      "title": "musings",
      "layoutId": "standard",
      "tags": [
        "page"
      ],
      "includes": [
        "common-footer"
      ],
      "zones": {
        "title": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "html": "musings"
          }
        ],
        "main": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "html": "<p class='w3-large'>These ideas are only half-baked, or maybe even more raw than that. But they are recorded here because I shall forget them otherwise. It's a sign of age.</p><div class='w3-section' id='headings_menu'></div><div class=\"w3-row-padding w3-stretch\"><div class=\"w3-twothird \"><h2>My half-baked idea 1</h2><p>This would be some kind of explanation of some kind of idea, with a picture to accompany it. I'd like to come up with a more dynamic iterator for these itesms. Does iterated content need to contain zones? That's a key question. At the moment, the inner content is rendered up-front so that the zones can be parsed. I definitely want to be able to render the content later. So the question is really... do I want to parse zones from dynamically rendered content? Would need more robust reference and dependency management - it's easy at the moment as I only have to add and not remove.<p></div><div class=\"w3-third w3-padding-16\">\n                <div class=\"w3-display-container w3-container w3-padding-16 w3-card w3-center undefined\">\n                    <img src=\"./img/img2.jpg\" class=\"w3-image\" style=\"width: 100%\">\n                    \n                        <div class=\"w3-display-middle w3-container w3-padding-16 w3-display-hover w3-normal w3-round-large w3-opacity-min w3-white w3-text-white\">pic 2</div>\n                        <div class=\"w3-display-middle w3-container w3-padding-16 w3-display-hover w3-normal w3-animate-opacity w3-text-black\">pic 2</div>\n                        \n                </div>\n            </div></div><div class=\"w3-row-padding w3-stretch\"><div class=\"w3-third w3-padding-16\">\n                <div class=\"w3-display-container w3-container w3-padding-16 w3-card w3-center undefined\">\n                    <img src=\"./img/img1.jpg\" class=\"w3-image\" style=\"width: 100%\">\n                    \n                        <div class=\"w3-display-middle w3-container w3-padding-16 w3-display-hover w3-normal w3-round-large w3-opacity-min w3-white w3-text-white\">pic 1</div>\n                        <div class=\"w3-display-middle w3-container w3-padding-16 w3-display-hover w3-normal w3-animate-opacity w3-text-black\">pic 1</div>\n                        \n                </div>\n            </div><div class=\"w3-twothird \"><h2>My half-baked idea 2</h2><p>This would be some kind of explanation of some kind of idea, with a picture to accompany it. I'd like to come up with a more dynamic iterator for these itesms. Does iterated content need to contain zones? That's a key question. At the moment, the inner content is rendered up-front so that the zones can be parsed. I definitely want to be able to render the content later. So the question is really... do I want to parse zones from dynamically rendered content? Would need more robust reference and dependency management - it's easy at the moment as I only have to add and not remove.<p></div></div><div class=\"w3-row-padding w3-stretch\"><div class=\"w3-twothird \"><h2>My half-baked idea 3</h2><p>This would be some kind of explanation of some kind of idea, with a picture to accompany it. I'd like to come up with a more dynamic iterator for these itesms. Does iterated content need to contain zones? That's a key question. At the moment, the inner content is rendered up-front so that the zones can be parsed. I definitely want to be able to render the content later. So the question is really... do I want to parse zones from dynamically rendered content? Would need more robust reference and dependency management - it's easy at the moment as I only have to add and not remove.<p></div><div class=\"w3-third w3-padding-16\">\n                <div class=\"w3-display-container w3-container w3-padding-16 w3-card w3-center undefined\">\n                    <img src=\"./img/img2.jpg\" class=\"w3-image\" style=\"width: 100%\">\n                    \n                        <div class=\"w3-display-middle w3-container w3-padding-16 w3-display-hover w3-normal w3-round-large w3-opacity-min w3-white w3-text-white\">pic 2</div>\n                        <div class=\"w3-display-middle w3-container w3-padding-16 w3-display-hover w3-normal w3-animate-opacity w3-text-black\">pic 2</div>\n                        \n                </div>\n            </div></div>\n                <div class=\"w3-content w3-padding-16\" style=\"max-width: 70%\">\n                    <div class=\"w3-panel w3-card-4 w3-round-large w3-sand\">\n                        <p class=\"w3-left-align\"><i class=\"fa fa-quote-left w3-xlarge w3-text-black w3-opacity-max\"></i></p>\n                        <p class=\" w3-xlarge w3-serif w3-center\">if you believe you can, or if you believe you can't, you're right</p>\n                        <p class=\"w3-right-align\"><i class=\"fa fa-quote-right w3-xlarge w3-text-black w3-opacity-max\"></i></p>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            "
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "plexiform",
      "title": "plexiform",
      "layoutId": "standard",
      "tags": [
